<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="S4.T4.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-task RL is necessary for in-context adaptation.</span>
Comparison of Cross-task RL, single-task RL, and the base (Qwen3-8B) model across the six environments. <em id="S4.T4.18" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Cum. Reward</em> is the total reward over the sequence (<math id="S4.T4.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\sum_{i}r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\sum_{i}r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>); <em id="S4.T4.19" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gain</em> is the cross-task improvement from first to last as a percentage of the initial reward (<math id="S4.T4.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r_{N}-r_{1})/r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r_{N}-r_{1})/r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>); <em id="S4.T4.20" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Final Reward</em> is the reward on the last task (<math id="S4.T4.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>). Each entry averages over the three in-distribution training latents and over <math id="S4.T4.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per latent.</figcaption>
</figure>
