<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span><span id="S4.T7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization under environment shift (OOD-2).</span>
A leave-one-out cross-task model, trained on all environments <em id="S4.T7.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">except</em> the evaluation one, beats the base on every held-out environment, with an average improvement of 14% on cumulative reward.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Exploration vs. exploitation efficiency.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The aggregate gains in Tables <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Cross-Task RL induces adaptation. ‣ 4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>–<a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Cross-Task RL induces adaptation. ‣ 4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> do not reveal whether Cross-Task RL’s lift comes from better exploration, better exploitation, or both. We isolate the two on Number Guessing with the agent-switching experiment from Section <a href="#S2" title="2 A Controllable Suite for Cross-Task Experiential Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Exploration vs. exploitation efficiency. ‣ 4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>): at a switch point <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{2,4,6,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{2,4,6,8\}</annotation></semantics></math>, control is handed from one agent (the <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">explorer</em>, running on tasks <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math>) to a second agent (the <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exploiter</em>, running on tasks <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K+1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K+1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math>), which inherits the running history accumulated by the first. Writing <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CT}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ST}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ST</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ST}</annotation></semantics></math> for the Cross-Task and Single-task RL agents and using the post-switch reward <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\cdot\!\to\!\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\cdot\!\to\!\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> of Section <a href="#S2" title="2 A Controllable Suite for Cross-Task Experiential Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we report the exploration and exploitation gains of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CT}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ST}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ST</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ST}</annotation></semantics></math> with the reference role held at <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\{\mathrm{CT},\mathrm{ST}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>CT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ST</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\{\mathrm{CT},\mathrm{ST}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}=\frac{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{CT}\!\to\!C)-R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{ST}\!\to\!C)}{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{ST}\!\to\!C)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ExploreGain</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>CT</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ST</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ST</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}=\frac{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{CT}\!\to\!C)-R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{ST}\!\to\!C)}{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(\mathrm{ST}\!\to\!C)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}=\frac{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{CT})-R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{ST})}{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{ST})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ExploitGain</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>CT</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ST</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>tail</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ST</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}=\frac{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{CT})-R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{ST})}{R_{\mathrm{tail}}(C\!\to\!\mathrm{ST})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">each a percentage of the reference’s tail reward. <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ExploreGain</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> holds the exploiter at <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and swaps the explorer; <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ExploitGain</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> holds the explorer at <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and swaps the exploiter (Table <a href="#S4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Exploration vs. exploitation efficiency. ‣ 4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Cross-Task RL has a positive exploration advantage at every <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, but it is small: between <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>17.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> depending on the exploiter, with a mild increasing trend in <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as more of the sequence is built before the switch. The exploitation advantage is far larger and present at every <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>: holding the explorer fixed, switching the exploiter from Single-task RL to Cross-Task RL adds between <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30\%</annotation></semantics></math> in tail reward, with values decreasing in <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> as the post-switch tail shrinks and there is less room for exploitation to compound. On Number Guessing, the exploitation gap therefore dominates the exploration gap by a factor of roughly <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="30\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30\times</annotation></semantics></math> and is the larger driver of Cross-Task RL’s lift. The same overall pattern, Cross-Task RL gaining on both axes simultaneously, holds across the other environments, though which axis dominates varies by environment (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
