<td id="A2.T9.5.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.13.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reward functional <math id="A2.T9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.T9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T9.5.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (cumulative return)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.14.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reference policy</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="A2.T9.5.14.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">frozen Qwen3-8B</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.15.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sampling temperature (training)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.T9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.16.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sampling top-<math id="A2.T9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (training)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.T9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.17" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.17.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sampling temperature (eval)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.T9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.70</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.70</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.18" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.T9.5.18.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Sampling top-<math id="A2.T9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (eval)</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.T9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T9.5.19" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T9.5.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T9.5.19.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Random seed</span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.5.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="263\ ([263,42,1729]\ \text{if multiple})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">263</mn><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">263</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">42</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1729</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.460em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">if multiple</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">263\ ([263,42,1729]\ \text{if multiple})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Single-environment Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of the five core environments (Number Guessing, Mastermind,
Hangman, Word Ladder, Secretary) we train two variants from the
shared Qwen3-8B base: a cross-task model
(<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=10</span>) and a single-task model (<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=1</span>). Both
variants train on the three in-distribution latents listed below
for each environment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number Guessing — <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">set_of_3</span>,
<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">set_of_2</span>, <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dynamic_range</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mastermind — <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">strictly_ascending</span>,
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">strictly_descending</span>, <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">first_is_6</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hangman — <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vowel_count_4</span>,
<span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">has_double_letter</span>, <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">starts_with_S</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Word Ladder — <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hub_word_4letter</span>,
<span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hub_word_3letter</span>, <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">order_outside_in</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secretary — <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">inverse_order</span>,
<span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fixed_position_2</span>, <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sorted_order</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Each training step samples a batch of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> prompts and generates
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts per prompt, where one rollout is a complete sequence of
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tasks. At every step the latent of each prompt is uniformly
sampled from the three training latents. cross-task models
therefore see <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 8\times 10=2{,}560" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2,560</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 8\times 10=2{,}560</annotation></semantics></math> task-episodes per
step, while single-task models see <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 8=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 8=256</annotation></semantics></math>. Training
proceeds for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> GRPO steps per run; we checkpoint
every 15 steps and select the best checkpoint by validation
cumulative return on a held-out seed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate each fine-tuned variant — and the base
Qwen3-8B model for comparison — under the same conditions
used during training (<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span> prompt and
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> feedback). For every environment we evaluate on
four latents: the three in-distribution latents seen during
training, together with one held-out (OOD-1) latent. The held-out
latents are:</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number Guessing — <span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">range_100</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mastermind — <span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">has_pair</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hangman — <span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ending_ABLE</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Word Ladder — <span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">order_left_to_right</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secretary — <span id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">best_is_last</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We run <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories of task-sequences per (model, environment,
latent) cell, for a total of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per environment for each model.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Multi-environment Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A single cross-task model
and a
single single-task model
are trained on
sequences sampled from the union of four core environments: Number
Guessing, Hangman, Word Ladder, and Secretary. Each sequence’s
environment is held fixed across its <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks (within-sequence
variation is over the latent’s task-specific <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, not over the
environment), and the sequence’s latent is uniformly sampled from
that environment’s two in-distribution training latents listed
below:</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number Guessing — <span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">set_of_3</span>,
<span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">range_100</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hangman — <span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vowel_count_4</span>,
<span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ending_ABLE</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Word Ladder — <span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hub_word_4letter</span>,
<span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hub_word_3letter</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secretary — <span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">inverse_order</span>,
<span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fixed_position_2</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Total training latents: <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> envs</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> latents</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=8</annotation></semantics></math>. Training proceeds for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="850" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>850</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">850</annotation></semantics></math> GRPO steps with the same
shared hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the two multi-environment fine-tuned variants — and the
base Qwen3-8B model for comparison — with <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span> prompt and
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> feedback. Note that these are the same training conditions as the model trained on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> while the single-task model is trained on <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span> given that it does not access the previous history. Each model is evaluated on every one
of the four core environments separately, on the two
in-distribution training latents per environment listed above, with
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per (model, environment, latent)
cell, for a total of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per environment.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Multi-environment Prompt and Feedback Sweep Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same setup as the multi-environment experiments above
(four core environments — Number Guessing, Hangman, Word Ladder,
Secretary — with the same two in-distribution training latents per
environment listed in Section <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Multi-environment Experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, for a total of
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> envs</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> latents</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=8</annotation></semantics></math> training latents).
We train only cross-task models (<span id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=10</span>); for each of the
four (prompt, feedback) combinations</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{prompt},\text{feedback})\in\{\texttt{some\_info},\texttt{full\_info}\}\times\{\texttt{standard},\texttt{information}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>prompt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>feedback</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">some_info</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">full_info</mtext><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">standard</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">information</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{prompt},\text{feedback})\in\{\texttt{some\_info},\texttt{full\_info}\}\times\{\texttt{standard},\texttt{information}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we train three independent models with seeds
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{42,263,1729\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>42,263</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1729</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{42,263,1729\}</annotation></semantics></math>, for a total of
<math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\text{ combos}\times 3\text{ seeds}=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> combos</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> seeds</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\text{ combos}\times 3\text{ seeds}=12</annotation></semantics></math> models. Training
proceeds for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="450" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>450</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">450</annotation></semantics></math> GRPO steps per model with the same shared
hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each fine-tuned model — and the base Qwen3-8B for comparison — is
evaluated on every one of the four prompt <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> feedback
combinations (yielding both in-distribution and cross-condition
cells), on every one of the four core environments, on the two
in-distribution training latents per environment, with <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math>
trajectories of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per
(model, environment, latent, eval-prompt, eval-feedback) cell.
This gives <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}\times 4\text{ eval combos}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> envs</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> latents</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> eval combos</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}\times 4\text{ eval combos}=32</annotation></semantics></math> eval cells per model and a total of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}600</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per
model.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Leave-one-out Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same setup as the multi-environment experiments above,
except that one environment <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is held out at a time. For each
held-out <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e\in\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\{</annotation></semantics></math>NG, hangman, wordladder, secretary<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math> we train
one cross-task model
on sequences sampled from the <em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">other three</em> environments, using
the same two in-distribution training latents per training
environment listed in Section <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Multi-environment Experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> (total
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> envs</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> latents</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\text{ envs}\times 2\text{ latents}=6</annotation></semantics></math> training latents per
leave-one-out model). The held-out environment <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> itself is never
seen at training time.
Training proceeds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="650" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>650</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">650</annotation></semantics></math>
GRPO steps per leave-one-out model with the same shared
hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same evaluation setup as the multi-environment
experiments above (<span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span> prompt, <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span>
feedback, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per cell). The only
change is that each leave-one-out model — and the base
Qwen3-8B for comparison — is evaluated only on its
held-out environment <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>, on the two in-distribution latents of
that environment, for a total of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per held-out
environment. This is the OOD-2 setting reported in the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Two-latent Single-environment Prompt Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of three environments — Number Guessing, Word Ladder,
Secretary — we train one cross-task model (<span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=10</span>) on
sequences sampled from <em id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">two</em> in-distribution training latents
per environment (six models total, but each trained
independently on its own environment). The two-latent sets are:</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number Guessing — <span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">set_of_3</span>, <span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">range_100</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Word Ladder — <span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hub_word_4letter</span>,
<span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">restricted_vocab_4letter</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Secretary — <span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fixed_position_2</span>,
<span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">increasing_position</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">At every training step the latent of each prompt is uniformly
sampled from the two training latents of the corresponding
environment. Training uses the <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no_info</span> prompt and
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> feedback, and proceeds for <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math> GRPO
steps per model with the same shared hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate each fine-tuned model — and the base Qwen3-8B for
comparison — under the same conditions used during training
(<span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no_info</span> prompt, <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> feedback), on the
same two in-distribution latents seen during training, with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math>
trajectories of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per (model, latent) cell, for a
total of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per environment.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Data Collection vs. Data Utilization Experiments</h3>

<div id="A2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment uses the trained models from the
multi-environment experiments (Section <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Multi-environment Experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) — the
base model, the cross-task multi-env model, and the single-task
multi-env model — without further fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same evaluation setup as the multi-environment
experiments (Section <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Multi-environment Experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>; <span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span>
prompt, <span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> feedback, the two in-distribution
latents per environment, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per
cell). For each model pair <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(A,B)\in\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,B)\in\{</annotation></semantics></math>(base, single-task),
(base, cross-task), (single-task, cross-task)<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math> and each
switch point <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{2,4,6,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{2,4,6,8\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we run two directional
rollouts:</p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\rightarrow B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\rightarrow B</annotation></semantics></math>: model <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> acts during episodes
<math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\ldots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\ldots,K</annotation></semantics></math> and collects the trajectory; model <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>
inherits the cross-task context <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{&lt;K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{&lt;K}</annotation></semantics></math> and acts during
episodes <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{+}1,\ldots,10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{+}1,\ldots,10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\rightarrow A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\rightarrow A</annotation></semantics></math>: the reverse.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each model pair, switch point, and direction is evaluated on every
one of the four core environments separately. Solo baselines come
from each model’s standalone single-agent eval on the same grid.
All reported <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> values average across the two
in-distribution latents within each environment.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>Compute (Qwen3-8B Training and Evaluation)</h3>

<div id="A2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report cumulative wall-clock compute for all Qwen3-8B
fine-tunes and post-training evaluations in A100 80GB GPU-hours.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training (RL fine-tunes).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Per-environment experiments — <math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> environments <math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> variants (<span id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=10</span> and <span id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ne=1</span>) <math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>
fine-tunes. Total: <math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I6.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}630" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,630</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}630</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-environment experiments — <math id="A2.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> fine-tunes (one
cross-task, one single-task). Total: <math id="A2.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="330" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>330</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">330</annotation></semantics></math>
A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Leave-one-out experiments — <math id="A2.I6.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> leave-one-out fine-tunes.
Total: <math id="A2.I6.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I6.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="270" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>270</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">270</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I6.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt and feedback sweep experiments
(Section <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Multi-environment Prompt and Feedback Sweep Experiments ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>) — <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> prompt <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>
feedback combinations <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> seeds <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>
cross-task fine-tunes. Total: <math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I6.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}300</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I6.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I6.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I6.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training subtotal:</span> <math id="A2.I6.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I6.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4{,}530" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4,530</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4{,}530</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation (Qwen3-8B post-training).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each fine-tuned variant and the base Qwen3-8B are
evaluated on their respective grids (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per cell,
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> tasks per trajectory):</p>
<ul id="A2.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Per-environment evals (<math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> fine-tuned variants <math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> base
across <math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> environments): <math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I7.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="190" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>190</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">190</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-env, leave-one-out, and switch-point sweeps:
<math id="A2.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="140" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>140</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">140</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation subtotal:</span> <math id="A2.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.I7.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="330" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>330</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">330</annotation></semantics></math> A100-hours.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Total.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training and evaluation of all Qwen3-8B models in this paper
consumed approximately <math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math><math id="A2.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5{,}860" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5,860</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5{,}860</annotation></semantics></math> A100 80GB GPU-hours.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.8 </span>Frontier-Model Evaluation</h3>

<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate three production frontier models accessed through
OpenRouter:</p>
<ul id="A2.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">openai/gpt-4o</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">google/gemini-2.5-flash</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All three are queried at sampling temperature <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.7</annotation></semantics></math>,
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">max_tokens<math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=4096" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>4096</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=4096</annotation></semantics></math></span> per response, with default top-<math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.
Routing to OpenRouter lets us evaluate every model through a single
unified API and avoids per-provider client differences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation grid.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the trained-model evaluations, the frontier-model evaluation
exercises the full prompt <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> feedback grid in order to test
each model under all of <span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no_info</span>, <span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span>, and
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">full_info</span> prompts and both <span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">standard</span> and
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">information</span> feedback conditions. For every (model,
environment) pair we evaluate on <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> latents <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> prompts
<math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> feedbacks <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories
<math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="120" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>120</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">120</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories per environment. The four eval latents are the four canonical latents
per environment listed in Section <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Environment Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Results</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix we show additional results for the <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exploration vs. exploitation efficiency</em> analysis in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for Number Guessing. For all experiments we follow the same agent-switching protocol. First, we compare Cross-Task RL against the <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">base</em> Qwen3-8B model on Number Guessing, alongside the corresponding agent-switch trajectory plot. Second, we report the Cross-Task RL vs. Single-task RL agent-switching tables for three additional environments (Hangman, Secretary, and Word Ladder) to test whether the exploration/exploitation decomposition behaves consistently across the benchmark.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Number Guessing: Cross-Task RL vs. base.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Word Ladder. ‣ C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reports the same protocol as Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> but with the base Qwen3-8B model in place of Single-task RL. Both gaps are dramatically larger than against Single-task RL, reaching <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+192.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>192.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+192.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> on exploration and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+189.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>189.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+189.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> on exploitation. Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Word Ladder. ‣ C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows the corresponding trajectories.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hangman.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Word Ladder. ‣ C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows that on Hangman, Cross-Task RL leads on both axes, with exploration advantages of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+20\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+62\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>62</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+62\%</annotation></semantics></math> and exploitation advantages of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+34\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>34</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+34\%</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike Number Guessing, exploration is the larger of the two on this environment, and it grows with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> while exploitation shrinks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Secretary.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Word Ladder. ‣ C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows a more balanced picture: exploration advantages of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+40\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+40\%</annotation></semantics></math> and exploitation advantages of <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+12\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+12\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>33</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+33\%</annotation></semantics></math>, with neither axis dominating consistently across switch points.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Word Ladder.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Word Ladder. ‣ C.1 Exploration efficiency vs. Exploitation efficiency ‣ Appendix C Additional Results" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> shows that on Word Ladder both gaps are small (under <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 4\%</annotation></semantics></math>), reflecting the convergence of Cross-Task RL and Single-task RL on this environment noted in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Demonstration: Cross-task RL for In-context Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Two patterns are consistent across environments. First, Cross-Task RL generally posts non-negative advantages on <em id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">both</em> exploration and exploitation, demonstrating that it improves both capabilities. Second, which axis dominates is environment-dependent: exploitation on Number Guessing, exploration on Hangman, mixed on Secretary, neither on Word Ladder. This suggests that Cross-Task RL addresses different bottlenecks depending on the structure of the task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.15306v1/base__VS__v1_4envs_ne10_per_env_number_guessing.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/120;" width="476" height="120"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Agent-switching: sequence RL vs. base Qwen3-8B on Number Guessing.<span id="A3.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The same asymmetry holds: sequence RL recovers most of its solo trajectory even when the early context was built by the base model, while the base model cannot exploit a context built by sequence RL. </span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.T10" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T10.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T10.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.7pt 8.0pt;"><span id="A3.T10.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Switch point <math id="A3.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.7pt 8.0pt;"><span id="A3.T10.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reference <math id="A3.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.7pt 8.0pt;"><math id="A3.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ExploreGain</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploreGain}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A3.T10.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.7pt 8.0pt;"><math id="A3.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ExploitGain</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ExploitGain}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T10.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
