<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span><span id="A3.T11.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Task RL vs. Single-task RL on <span id="A3.T11.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hangman</span></span> (4-latent average). All values positive: Cross-Task RL is both a better explorer and a better exploiter than Single-task RL, with the exploration advantage growing in <math id="A3.T11.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and the exploitation advantage shrinking as the post-switch tail shrinks.</figcaption>
</figure>
