<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Adaptation Breakdown</h3>

<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Adaptation Breakdown: Models ignore the hint of hidden pattern</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1419.44" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 1419.44" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1419.44) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#445277;" fill="#445277" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.43 L 0 1415.01 C 0 1417.46 1.98 1419.44 4.43 1419.44 L 472.95 1419.44 C 475.39 1419.44 477.38 1417.46 477.38 1415.01 L 477.38 4.43 C 477.38 1.98 475.39 0 472.95 0 L 4.43 0 C 1.98 0 0 1.98 0 4.43 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9FB;" fill="#F9F9FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.97 4.43 L 0.97 1398.56 L 476.41 1398.56 L 476.41 4.43 C 476.41 2.52 474.86 0.97 472.95 0.97 L 4.43 0.97 C 2.52 0.97 0.97 2.52 0.97 4.43 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#50618D;" fill="#50618D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.97 1399.53 L 0.97 1415.01 C 0.97 1416.92 2.52 1418.47 4.43 1418.47 L 472.95 1418.47 C 474.86 1418.47 476.41 1416.92 476.41 1415.01 L 476.41 1399.53 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 15.98 1405.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="418.3"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.23em;">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">GPT-4o ignores the hint that there is a pattern</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 15.98 934.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.19em;--ltx-fo-height:32.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:66.78em;font-size:10pt;" height="1378.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 454.67)" width="445.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.19em;">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Configuration:</span><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Environment: number_guessing. Latent: set_of_3. Prompt: some_info. Feedback: standard. Trajectory: 0.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Setup.<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> On set_of_3 the targets cycle through three fixed values. With <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">some_info</span>, GPT-4o is told a pattern exists. Yet the opening guess is the midpoint of the search range and the agent never tries one of the previously-seen targets first.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What went wrong.<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The set-of-3 hypothesis is never voiced or tested. Behavior is identical to the <span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no_info</span> regime.</span></span></span>
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Per-task summary<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (<math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p8.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> marks tasks whose transcript is shown below</span>).</span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Agent task is to identify a hidden integer between 1 and 1000; after each guess, the game master replies whether the target is greater than, less than, or equal to the guess.</span></span>
</span>
